### **📝 Problem Statement: Gearbox & Shaft Design**

A motor drives an input shaft carrying a spur gear at a speed of **$1200\text{ RPM}$** with a power input of **$15\text{ kW}$**. The motor pinion (**Gear A**) has **$20\text{ teeth}$** and meshes with a driven gear (**Gear B**) having **$60\text{ teeth}$** mounted on an output shaft.

Assuming a mechanical efficiency of **$100\%$**, perform the following calculations:

#### **1. Gear Analysis:**

* Calculate the gear ratio ($i$).


* Calculate the output speed ($\text{RPM}_{\text{out}}$) of Gear B.


* Calculate the output torque ($T_{\text{out}}$) available at the output shaft in $\text{N}\cdot\text{m}$.



#### **2. Shaft Analysis:**

* If the output shaft transmits this output torque ($T_{\text{out}}$) and is subjected to an equivalent bending moment of $M = 250\text{ N}\cdot\text{m}$, calculate the minimum required shaft diameter ($d$) using the von Mises shear stress criterion.



#### **3. Material Specification:**

* The shaft is made of steel with an allowable shear stress ($\tau_{\text{allow}}$) of **$50\text{ MPa}$**. (thread_id: eaa4ca4d-e408-4597-9180-12e2794dba86)
